### Changes Made (4 total)

**Internal Flow Fixes (1):**
- Rituals section: moved the faceless-era paragraph out of its old slot (it sat *after* the "Watch what he kept" adult-architecture pivot, yanking chronology backward right before Tampa). It now lives in the hiding-theme block, so the seams read "told no one for a decade" → "The hiding went further than the rituals," then "The last ritual he did not choose was gone" → "Watch what he kept," and the section closes on the adult-architecture pivot that feeds the Tampa section directly.

**Transition Fixes (3):**
- Tampa → Money: was a hard cut from the Ludwig quote straight into a table. Added a bridge carrying the "easiest job" keyword: *"The easiest job there is paid accordingly. What Charlie did with the money is the part that needs explaining."*
- Money → Judge: the section's central paradox (a man who pays to stay undisturbed working as a professional judge of disturbances) was implied by the H2 but never stated. Added: *"That makes the day job strange. The man guarding that surface spends it ruling on other people's chaos."* It carries "surface" from the Money section's last line.
- Judge section, Mitchell → Rizzo: the jump from the Brisbane courtroom to esports-ownership testimonials had no connector. Added: *"The same protective instinct runs his own house."*

### What Was Preserved
- All frontmatter, working-notes comments, Svelte/HTML blocks, internal links, and the table
- The cold open, diagnosis section, money-ledger framing, Naroditsky section, and ending untouched (all strong; the ending's rituals→bits-number callback is the best transition in the piece)
- The Diagnosis → Rituals and Bothered → Naroditsky boundaries left alone: both open on dated scenes, which is this piece's house style, and the "twelve years old" callback / section-title setup carry them adequately

